1
00:00:06,146 --> 00:00:08,767
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

2
00:00:08,936 --> 00:00:14,580
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

3
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:22,872
After the Baiyah(بَيْعة), given to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه in the portico,

4
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:28,403
the Saqeefah(ثقيفه) of Bannu Sa'adah(بنوسعدة), the following day, Tuesday.

5
00:00:29,968 --> 00:00:34,481
They met in the Masjid(مسجد) and that was the Al-Baiyah-Al-Aamah(ألبيعة العامة)

6
00:00:34,506 --> 00:00:39,118
that's when everybody was going to give the Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

7
00:00:39,561 --> 00:00:44,644
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) stand on the Mimber(ممبر), the pulpit.

8
00:00:45,779 --> 00:00:53,057
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه After praising Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ and making Salah(صلاة) on the messenger of Allah ﷺ,

9
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:53,729
he said;

10
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:59,505
Yesterday I have said something that's not in the book of Allah and it was my own opinion.

11
00:01:00,922 --> 00:01:04,475
This statement that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said that Muhammadﷺ did not die.

12
00:01:05,657 --> 00:01:08,842
And the things that were relating to that, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

13
00:01:08,867 --> 00:01:12,547
It's not from the book of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ, it was my opinion.

14
00:01:13,633 --> 00:01:17,552
So he was apologizing for what he has said, the day before.

15
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:25,892
And then he asked the Muslims to stand up and give Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

16
00:01:27,057 --> 00:01:30,239
So the one, who would carry the initiative,

17
00:01:30,574 --> 00:01:34,399
in a lot of the major events of the Ummah(امة) was Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

18
00:01:35,873 --> 00:01:40,248
He was the first one, to put his hand in the hand of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) in the Saqeefah(ثقيفة) and give him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

19
00:01:40,738 --> 00:01:46,613
And now he is the one, who is arranging the general Baiyah(بَيْعة) of the Muslims.

20
00:01:46,638 --> 00:01:49,790
So the Muslims started standing up one by one,

21
00:01:50,395 --> 00:01:54,296
placing their hand in the hand of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and giving him Baiyah(بَيْعة).

22
00:01:54,755 --> 00:01:55,924
What does Baiyah(بَيْعة) mean?

23
00:01:56,948 --> 00:01:59,740
The literal meaning of Baiyah(بَيْعة) is, a transaction, a sale.

24
00:01:59,997 --> 00:02:03,458
If I sell you something that transaction is called Baiyah(بَيْعة).

25
00:02:04,046 --> 00:02:13,729
So that word was borrowed, in this context, to carry a new meaning, and that is a covenant between two parties.

26
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:18,921
Just like in a financial transaction, you have two parties,

27
00:02:18,946 --> 00:02:22,346
and both parties consent to this trade.

28
00:02:22,812 --> 00:02:29,597
 I mean, there must be consent, when there's a financial transaction that happens.

29
00:02:30,473 --> 00:02:35,638
I cannot sell you this, if I don't want to, and you will not buy it, if you don't want it.

30
00:02:36,051 --> 00:02:45,897
So, both parties agree and they would shake hands, to finalize that agreement.

31
00:02:46,435 --> 00:02:51,330
So the shaking of the hand, symbolizes the agreement of both sides.

32
00:02:52,063 --> 00:02:56,435
It means that both of us agree and we do that by the shaking of the hand.

33
00:02:57,484 --> 00:03:02,555
And even until this day, this tradition carries on among Muslims and non Muslims

34
00:03:03,519 --> 00:03:05,995
the deal is finalized by the shaking of the hand.

35
00:03:07,130 --> 00:03:15,408
So that meaning was borrowed and was used to refer to the relationship between the leader and the followers,

36
00:03:15,844 --> 00:03:17,570
 and the covenant that is between them.

37
00:03:19,163 --> 00:03:19,978
And that is Baiyah(بَيْعة),

38
00:03:20,042 --> 00:03:22,621
it's a pledge of an allegiance to a leader.

39
00:03:23,911 --> 00:03:29,580
Rasool Allah ﷺ took a Baiyah(بَيْعة) from the Ansaar رضي الله عنهم in Baiyah-Tul-Aqabah(بيعة العقبة)

40
00:03:30,427 --> 00:03:32,679
and he took a pledge of allegiance from women

41
00:03:33,187 --> 00:03:35,633
and he took pledge of allegiance from individuals

42
00:03:37,437 --> 00:03:41,919
he took a pledge of allegiance from one man, that you don't ask anybody for anything.

43
00:03:44,639 --> 00:03:46,967
And the pledge could be on different issues.

44
00:03:48,109 --> 00:03:51,097
So Baiyah(بَيْعة), there's a minor Baiyah(بَيْعة) and there's a major Baiyah(بَيْعة).

45
00:03:51,795 --> 00:03:54,733
A minor Baiyah(بَيْعة) is on a particular issue.

46
00:03:55,274 --> 00:03:57,495
While the major Baiyah(بَيْعة) is on the Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

47
00:03:58,438 --> 00:04:00,679
The major Baiyah(بَيْعة) is the Khilafah(خِلَافَه)

48
00:04:01,259 --> 00:04:05,621
And that is where the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, that's the context of the Hadith(حديث).

49
00:04:06,222 --> 00:04:10,625
من مات وليس في عنقه بيعة مات ميْتَةً جاهلية

50
00:04:11,067 --> 00:04:13,478
If you die and you don't have a Baiyah(بَيْعة) in your neck.

51
00:04:13,712 --> 00:04:16,973
Then you're dying on the way of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة), the way of ignorance, pre Islam.

52
00:04:17,291 --> 00:04:20,801
And notice the word here, - "في رقبة", - In his neck,

53
00:04:21,262 --> 00:04:23,898
Baiyah(بَيْعة) is some things that you can't get out of, if you enter

54
00:04:25,135 --> 00:04:30,797
Baiyah(بَيْعة) is something that there's no way of a breaking it.

55
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:35,646
And if a person commits to it, they must commit to it until the rest of their life.

56
00:04:36,731 --> 00:04:41,317
And that's why Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It's like tied around your neck, you can't get it out.

57
00:04:42,803 --> 00:04:45,803
So when the Sahabah(صحابه) would give Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه Baiyah(بَيْعة),

58
00:04:45,828 --> 00:04:47,057
they know that it's a serious thing.

59
00:04:47,661 --> 00:04:51,353
And when they gave the Baiyah(بَيْعة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ before that, they knew it's a serious thing.

60
00:04:52,498 --> 00:04:58,155
So when the Ansaar(أنْصَار) were told by Rasool Allah ﷺ I want you to give me the Baiyah(بَيْعة),

61
00:04:58,374 --> 00:05:02,493
that you would protect me from what you protect your families and wealth.

62
00:05:03,063 --> 00:05:06,004
The Ansaar(أنْصَار) knew the implications of that.

63
00:05:07,527 --> 00:05:12,511
So one of them stood up before they give the Baiyah(بَيْعة), and he told the Ansaar(أنْصَار).

64
00:05:13,134 --> 00:05:14,847
Do you know what you're getting into?

65
00:05:17,172 --> 00:05:21,756
 This is something that will cause you a lot of enemies,

66
00:05:23,629 --> 00:05:26,238
and people are going to point their source towards you.

67
00:05:27,650 --> 00:05:30,499
So he's telling them, this thing that we're about to do right now.

68
00:05:30,539 --> 00:05:31,505
And then he said;

69
00:05:32,102 --> 00:05:34,731
If you feel that you're not able to carry it out.

70
00:05:35,203 --> 00:05:37,891
Pull out of it now before it's too late.

71
00:05:39,658 --> 00:05:41,617
Because after we give the Baiyah(بَيْعة), we can't walk out.

72
00:05:43,252 --> 00:05:47,436
So they asked Rasool Allah ﷺ, that's what you want from us, what's our part of the agreement

73
00:05:47,461 --> 00:05:49,479
because Baiyah(بَيْعة) is a two way thing.

74
00:05:50,034 --> 00:05:52,915
It's not a one way relationship, it's two ways.

75
00:05:53,796 --> 00:05:56,912
So they said that you're part of the agreement, what is ours,

76
00:05:56,937 --> 00:05:58,956
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not promise them Kingdom,

77
00:05:59,037 --> 00:06:01,481
did not promise them a salary, did not promise them wealth.

78
00:06:01,625 --> 00:06:04,355
He said: "لكم الجنة" , I promise you paradise.

79
00:06:05,790 --> 00:06:06,183
They said:

80
00:06:06,256 --> 00:06:08,534
 "رابح بيعة لا نقيل ولا نستقيل"

81
00:06:08,719 --> 00:06:10,498
They said: What a profitable trade.

82
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:12,070
We will never give up.

83
00:06:12,670 --> 00:06:13,731
What's better than Jannah(جنة).

84
00:06:18,168 --> 00:06:23,958
So the Baiyah(بَيْعة) that was referring to in this Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ is the Baiyah(بَيْعة) of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

85
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:28,517
And this type of Baiyah(بَيْعة) should only be given to the Khalifah(خليفه),

86
00:06:28,542 --> 00:06:29,802
it's not given to anyone else.

87
00:06:29,831 --> 00:06:32,404
So the major Baiyah(بَيْعة) only goes to the Khalifah(خليفه)

88
00:06:32,995 --> 00:06:37,107
minor Baiyah(بَيْعة) on other issues can be given to other people,

89
00:06:37,326 --> 00:06:39,267
like for example in the Battle of Yarmook,

90
00:06:39,702 --> 00:06:40,640
 "تبايعن على الموت"

91
00:06:40,708 --> 00:06:45,189
Some of the Sahabah(صحابه) said: We pledge to die, it was a Baiyah(بَيْعة) to die in this battle.

92
00:06:45,866 --> 00:06:49,984
So this form of Baiyah(بَيْعة) is acceptable in the absence of a Khalifah(خليفه),

93
00:06:50,329 --> 00:06:54,325
but the major Baiyah(بَيْعة) only belongs to the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims,

94
00:06:54,350 --> 00:06:56,567
I hope that this issue of Baiyah(بَيْعة) is clear.

95
00:06:59,255 --> 00:07:04,361
After they give the Baiyah(بَيْعة) Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه stood up on the Mimber(ممبر),

96
00:07:04,401 --> 00:07:06,760
 and he delivered his inauguration speech.

97
00:07:07,326 --> 00:07:12,974
The first speech that he gives as the Khalifah(خليفه). He said:

98
00:07:13,881 --> 00:07:23,755
أما بعدُ، أَيُّها الناسُ فَإِني قد وُلِّيتُ عليكم ولست بخيركم فإِنْ أَحْسَنْتُ فَأَعِينُونِي وإِنْ أَسَأْتُ فَقَوِّمُوني

99
00:07:24,142 --> 00:07:31,638
الصِدْقُ أمانةٌ والكَذِبُ خِيَانَةٌ ، والضعيفُ فيكم قويٌّ عندي حتى أرجعَ إليه حقَّه إن شاء اللّه

100
00:07:32,485 --> 00:07:37,085
، والقويّ فيكم ضعيفٌ عندي حتى آخذَ الحقَّ منه إن شاء اللّه

101
00:07:37,769 --> 00:07:42,700
لا يَدَعُ قومٌ الجِهادَ في سبيل اللّه إلا خَذَلَهم اللَّهُ بالذُلِّ

102
00:07:43,162 --> 00:07:46,987
ولا تَشِيعُ الفاحشةُ في قومٍ إِلا عَمَّهم اللَّهُ بِالبلاءِ

103
00:07:47,718 --> 00:07:57,781
،  أَطِيعُوني ما أَطَعْتُ اللَّهَ ورسولَه فإِذا عَصَيْت اللَّهَ ورسولَه فلا طاعةَ لي عليكم ،  قُومُوا إلى صلاتكم يَرْحَمْكُمُ اللّه

104
00:07:58,978 --> 00:08:00,427
He said: "أَيُّها الناسُ" , O people!

105
00:08:01,432 --> 00:08:06,816
I have been put in authority over you, and I'm not the best of you.

106
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:11,250
So if I do the right thing, then help me.

107
00:08:11,561 --> 00:08:19,407
And if I do wrong, then put me straight, truthfulness is a sacred trust and lying is a betrayal,

108
00:08:20,346 --> 00:08:23,390
 the weak one among you is strong as far as I'm concerned,

109
00:08:23,415 --> 00:08:26,031
until I restore to him his right; In Sha Allah(إن شاء الله)

110
00:08:26,581 --> 00:08:31,320
and the strong one of you is weak, until I take what is due from him; In Sha Allah(إن شاء الله).

111
00:08:32,739 --> 00:08:38,186
No people forsake Jihad(جهاد) in the way of Allah, but that Allah afflicts them with humiliation,

112
00:08:38,787 --> 00:08:41,831
nor does indecency ever spread among the people,

113
00:08:41,852 --> 00:08:44,128
but that Allah envelops them in punishment.

114
00:08:44,786 --> 00:08:48,096
Obey me as long as I obey Allah and His Messenger,

115
00:08:48,310 --> 00:08:52,879
and if I disobey Allah and His Messenger, then you do not owe me obedience.

116
00:08:54,223 --> 00:08:57,680
Stand up for your prayer, May Allah have mercy upon you.

117
00:09:00,555 --> 00:09:08,689
This is a masterpiece, when it comes to Islamic politics or governance.

118
00:09:10,482 --> 00:09:17,320
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is now charting a new territory, he is the first Khalifah(خليفه).

119
00:09:18,625 --> 00:09:23,194
No one has experienced in that before that it was Rasool Allah ﷺ.

120
00:09:24,026 --> 00:09:29,322
Now obviously there is going to be some difference between a Nabi(نَبِي) leading his people,

121
00:09:30,425 --> 00:09:34,570
and one of the people leading them, there are some differences.

122
00:09:35,693 --> 00:09:38,287
So now Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is the one,

123
00:09:38,312 --> 00:09:42,817
who will be laying down the ground rules for the Khulafaa(خلفاء) after him.

124
00:09:43,701 --> 00:09:46,395
He is the one, who will set the Sunnah(سنة) of Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

125
00:09:47,030 --> 00:09:48,372
No one has done it before.

126
00:09:49,154 --> 00:09:53,964
He is the one who's gonna lay down the groundwork for Khilafah-Al-Islamia(خلافةالإسلامية).

127
00:09:55,417 --> 00:09:59,573
And this falls under the Sunnah(سنة) which we are ordered by Rasool Allah ﷺ to follow

128
00:09:59,677 --> 00:10:07,577
because he said: Follow my Sunnah(سنة) and the Sunnah(سنة) of the righteous guided Khulafah(خلفاء), after me.

129
00:10:08,993 --> 00:10:15,806
So what Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is doing, is part of the Sunnah(سنة) that we are commanded to follow.

130
00:10:18,527 --> 00:10:23,399
There are a lot of issues that could be debated, on how to deal with?

131
00:10:23,615 --> 00:10:26,537
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه from the first day

132
00:10:26,928 --> 00:10:29,565
is telling them this is how we are going to do it.

133
00:10:30,688 --> 00:10:34,485
First of all, he started by saying, I have been put in authority over you,

134
00:10:34,789 --> 00:10:36,157
and I'm not the best of you.

135
00:10:36,835 --> 00:10:41,816
Now he is the best of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم no doubt about that.

136
00:10:42,330 --> 00:10:46,322
But this could also mean that there could be a situation

137
00:10:46,674 --> 00:10:53,025
where the Imam(اِمَام), might not be the best out of the community.

138
00:10:53,786 --> 00:10:57,282
If that is the case do you change the Imam(اِمَام), or do you follow the Imam(اِمَام).

139
00:10:58,670 --> 00:10:59,295
And this is called,

140
00:10:59,335 --> 00:11:00,990
"إمامة الفاضل على المفضول"

141
00:11:01,404 --> 00:11:06,752
The Imamah(إمامة), of the Mafdhool(مفضول) is not the best, over the best.

142
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:14,116
The Scholars say that if this Imam(اِمَام) is following the law of Allah,

143
00:11:14,515 --> 00:11:16,966
and establishing the Hudood(حدود) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

144
00:11:18,857 --> 00:11:23,158
then the people should not pull out their hands from his Baiyah(بَيْعة).

145
00:11:25,951 --> 00:11:29,022
So even though he might not be the best, he could be the second best,

146
00:11:29,416 --> 00:11:32,311
but as long as he's establishing the Shariah(شريعة) of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ,

147
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:35,545
people should follow that Imam(اِمَام) to avoid Fitnah(فِتْنَه).

148
00:11:38,265 --> 00:11:43,046
And that could be implied from the statement of Abu Bakr that I'm not the best among you,

149
00:11:44,179 --> 00:11:46,167
even though I'm the Khalifah(خليفه) but I'm not the best among you.

150
00:11:47,139 --> 00:11:50,111
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said this out of humbleness.

151
00:11:53,865 --> 00:11:58,560
He establishes the sources of law, in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

152
00:11:58,900 --> 00:12:00,938
he was receiving the Wahii(وحي) from Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ

153
00:12:01,027 --> 00:12:02,628
and that is how he would govern the Ummah(امة).

154
00:12:03,229 --> 00:12:06,875
What should do Khalifah(خليفه) after him do, what are the sources of law.?

155
00:12:07,869 --> 00:12:09,688
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه says,

156
00:12:10,050 --> 00:12:13,017
أَطِيعُوني ما أَطَعْتُ اللَّهَ ورسوله

157
00:12:14,207 --> 00:12:21,779
And now, obey me, as long as I am obeying Allah and His messenger.

158
00:12:21,804 --> 00:12:23,452
So what are the sources of law.?

159
00:12:23,935 --> 00:12:29,135
Allah, His words Qur'an and His Messenger, the Sunnah(سنة) of Muhammadﷺ.

160
00:12:29,592 --> 00:12:33,686
So the sources of law in Islamic government are Qur'an and Sunnah(سنة),

161
00:12:34,416 --> 00:12:36,842
أَطِيعُوني ما أَطَعْتُ اللَّهَ ورسوله

162
00:12:37,432 --> 00:12:41,420
Follow me, as long as I am following Allah and His messenger.

163
00:12:45,468 --> 00:12:50,472
Number two, and I'm dissecting the speech of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

164
00:12:51,148 --> 00:12:53,610
Number two, so we talked about the sources of law.

165
00:12:53,650 --> 00:12:54,442
Number two,

166
00:12:55,211 --> 00:12:58,748
the right of the Ummah(امة), to hold the leaders accountable.

167
00:13:00,596 --> 00:13:04,170
Does the Ummah(امة), have the right to hold the leaders accountable.

168
00:13:04,565 --> 00:13:07,969
This is not a clear issue yet, at that moment.

169
00:13:08,066 --> 00:13:11,601
Because in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ obviously they cannot,

170
00:13:12,379 --> 00:13:16,939
in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ the Ummah(امة) cannot hold Rasool Allah ﷺ accountable.

171
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:22,778
Who are the Ummah(امة) to hold the Messenger of Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ accountable for what he does.

172
00:13:23,775 --> 00:13:28,751
So the Ummah(امة) does not have the right to question the leadership of Muhammadﷺ.

173
00:13:30,215 --> 00:13:33,489
Because Muhammadﷺ was being corrected by Jibreel عليه السّلام.

174
00:13:36,175 --> 00:13:38,801
In the case of the Ibn-Maktoum(إبن مكتوم),

175
00:13:39,235 --> 00:13:43,490
يا أيُّها النبيُّ لم تُحَرِّم مَا أَحَلَّ اللهُ لَكَ  , عَفَا اللَّهُ عَنْكَ لِمَ أَذِنْتَ لَهُمْ

176
00:13:43,711 --> 00:13:47,718
All of these are examples where Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ is correcting Muhammadﷺ through Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل).

177
00:13:48,496 --> 00:13:51,671
But the people do not have a right to correct Muhammadﷺ, the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah.

178
00:13:53,011 --> 00:13:55,136
So, now this is an issue that needs to be clarified.

179
00:13:55,472 --> 00:14:00,186
Now Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is not a Nabi(نَبِي), can the people, correct me or not.

180
00:14:01,811 --> 00:14:02,532
He said;

181
00:14:03,246 --> 00:14:07,400
"فإِنْ أَحْسَنْتُ فَأَعِينُونِي وإِنْ أَسَأْتُ فَقَوِّمُوني "

182
00:14:08,059 --> 00:14:14,215
So if I do right, then help me and support me and if I do wrong, then put me straight.

183
00:14:15,308 --> 00:14:18,346
If I do something wrong, then you have to put me straight.

184
00:14:19,014 --> 00:14:21,379
Now the leadership is not in the hands of a Nabi(نَبِي),

185
00:14:21,419 --> 00:14:24,373
so the person after the Nabi(نَبِي) can make mistakes.

186
00:14:24,952 --> 00:14:28,420
And if you ever see such a mistake, it is your responsibility to put me straight

187
00:14:29,027 --> 00:14:31,960
so he's telling them. Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق), if he want it,

188
00:14:32,784 --> 00:14:35,920
he could have set rules of dictatorship and tyranny,

189
00:14:37,402 --> 00:14:42,850
but Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه knows that his way will be the way that will be followed after him.

190
00:14:42,890 --> 00:14:48,702
 So he's saying that it is your responsibility to fix my mistakes, and the word,

191
00:14:48,742 --> 00:14:49,583
 "فَقَوِّمُوني"

192
00:14:50,349 --> 00:14:56,889
has connotations of putting me on the straight path even force is needed.

193
00:14:57,300 --> 00:14:57,878
"تقوين",

194
00:14:58,054 --> 00:15:01,960
Something is bent, you use your strength to make it straight.

195
00:15:03,248 --> 00:15:04,911
And once Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was saying,

196
00:15:05,255 --> 00:15:08,864
If I disobey Allah and go and divert from the straight path.

197
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:09,658
What will you do?

198
00:15:09,842 --> 00:15:13,343
One man stood up and said: We will straighten you, with our swords.

199
00:15:14,241 --> 00:15:18,416
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله) that among my people is somebody like you.

200
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:22,665
He didn't call for the executioner to come.

201
00:15:22,916 --> 00:15:25,228
He said: Al-Hamdolillah(ألحمدلله) that there's somebody among my people

202
00:15:25,475 --> 00:15:27,088
who can stand up and speak the truth.

203
00:15:28,011 --> 00:15:31,034
So, accountability of the leadership is necessary,

204
00:15:31,743 --> 00:15:35,703
