00:31:38,757 --> 00:31:41,768
Number two, the right of the Ummah(امة) to hold its leaders accountable.

414
00:31:42,069 --> 00:31:43,932
Number three, justice and equality.

415
00:31:44,232 --> 00:31:46,995
Number four, trust between the leader and the followers.

416
00:31:47,257 --> 00:31:49,230
Number five, Jihad(جهاد) Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله).

417
00:31:49,365 --> 00:31:52,158
Number Six, war against vice.

418
00:31:53,918 --> 00:31:58,600
One day Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and Abu Obaidah Ibn Jarrah(ابوعبيدة إبن جراح)

419
00:31:59,933 --> 00:32:01,541
after Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) became a Khalifah(خليفه).

420
00:32:02,319 --> 00:32:09,359
They saw him carrying some garments on his shoulder, and he's walking down to the marketplace to do business.

421
00:32:10,295 --> 00:32:11,876
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told him what are you doing?

422
00:32:12,610 --> 00:32:16,503
He said: I'm going to trade, buy and sell. He said;

423
00:32:16,528 --> 00:32:17,978
بعد أن وليت أمرالمسلمين

424
00:32:18,003 --> 00:32:21,937
After you became the, one responsible for the affairs of the Muslims.

425
00:32:22,167 --> 00:32:24,371
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is not saying because you are Khalifah(خليفه)

426
00:32:24,477 --> 00:32:27,483
