 The Ummah(امة) is paying the price,

748
00:53:33,048 --> 00:53:37,697
because it doesn't want to pay the tax, it's dues for having all of this.

749
00:53:38,162 --> 00:53:41,448
We want solutions for everything but you don't want to pay for anything.

750
00:53:44,547 --> 00:53:49,177
So the field of Islamic work is way undermanned

751
00:53:50,368 --> 00:53:53,045
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)  wanted the Khalifah(خليفه) to be there full time,

752
00:53:53,069 --> 00:53:55,029
the salary wasn't enough we're gonna give you more.

753
00:53:55,575 --> 00:53:57,244
Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said: Give him more.

754
00:53:58,712 --> 00:54:03,223
And in Islamic work if there is a salary to be paid,

755
00:54:03,383 --> 00:54:10,855
 it's going to be lower than what people can get from non Islamic work, that's why you get the lowest in qualification.

756
00:54:11,925 --> 00:54:15,315
Because if I can make a few $1,000 in another work.

757
00:54:15,339 --> 00:54:18,520
Why would I go and take the line of Islamic work.?

758
00:54:20,055 --> 00:54:23,561
I mean just because Islamic work doesn't mean that the person should be paid less.

759
00:54:23,872 --> 00:54:26,593
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه had some bills to pay,

760
00:54:26,785 --> 00:54:28,503
and he wanted the sufficient salary.

761
00:54:28,779 --> 00:54:31,160
If you're not gonna pay it I'm not gonna give my full time for it.

762
00:54:32,479 --> 00:54:36,530
He didn't say that, No! I should have Zuhd(زهد) and just accept whatever you give me. No!

763
00:54:37,097 --> 00:54:39,465
I have some needs that need to be taken care of.

764
00:54:40,031 --> 00:54:45,021
He wasn't asking for a pay raise because of the role of being the Khalifah(خليفه)

765
00:54:45,658 --> 00:54:48,736
He was asking for what he could get, if he wasn't the Khalifah(خليفه).

766
00:54:50,623 --> 00:54:53,191
These are my qualifications, I'm a successful businessman,

767
00:54:53,231 --> 00:54:56,619
I can go and buy and sell in the marketplace and I can make a living.

768
00:54:57,084 --> 00:55:00,105
Pay me equivalent to that, otherwise I can't fill this job.

769
00:55:00,444 --> 00:55:03,618
And when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) grabbed his hand, I forgot to mention this,

770
00:55:03,849 --> 00:55:05,749
when he told him, تعال ها هنا Come here

771
00:55:06,292 --> 00:55:07,100
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said:

772
00:55:08,199 --> 00:55:09,951
مالي أمرتكم حاجة

773
00:55:10,001 --> 00:55:12,594
I don't need this position of authority, you put me in.

774
00:55:13,175 --> 00:55:15,041
It's not paying me enough to take care of my family.

775
00:55:17,013 --> 00:55:18,651
I have a family to take care of.

776
00:55:19,969 --> 00:55:26,239
So Islamic work will remain unprofessional and weak, and the needs of the Muslim communities,

777
00:55:26,279 --> 00:55:31,003
 especially as minorities living in non Muslim societies.

778
00:55:31,229 --> 00:55:34,838
These needs are not going to be fulfilled unless the Muslim community comes together,

779
00:55:35,139 --> 00:55:38,755
pays money, brings the best people to take care of those needs.

780
00:55:39,665 --> 00:55:41,693
Bring the teachers, to teach Arabic and pay them well.

781
00:55:42,525 --> 00:55:44,806
Bring the Imam(اِمَام)s, to take care of the Masajid(مساجد).

782
00:55:45,560 --> 00:55:50,009
Bring the good administrators, the ones who are successful in the business world.

783
00:55:50,341 --> 00:55:53,146
Bring them into Islamic work so that they can bring their skills

784
00:55:53,369 --> 00:55:55,760
and run the Islamic organizations professionally.

785
00:55:56,140 --> 00:56:01,331
In the community Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, he was very active.

786
00:56:02,319 --> 00:56:09,171
He had one wife in Madina and he had another wife in As-Sunh(ألصنح),  a village outside of Madina.

787
00:56:11,767 --> 00:56:14,922
Before he was Khalifah(خليفه) he used to milk their goats.

788
00:56:15,901 --> 00:56:23,718
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه would go to these families, and milk their goats in his small village.

789
00:56:26,177 --> 00:56:28,444
So when he became Khalifah(خليفه) a young girl said:

790
00:56:28,507 --> 00:56:31,638
O Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is not going to milk our goats anymore.

791
00:56:32,138 --> 00:56:33,376
Now he's the Khalifah(خليفه)

792
00:56:34,462 --> 00:56:37,373
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه heard that and he said:

793
00:56:38,221 --> 00:56:42,800
No, I will still milk your goats, and I pray to Allah عَزَّوَجَلْ

794
00:56:43,500 --> 00:56:49,240
not to make this new position of mine, prevent me from doing what I used to do before.

795
00:56:50,766 --> 00:56:55,751
I don't want this position to change my Khuluq(خلق), to change what I used to do before

796
00:56:56,209 --> 00:57:02,644
and he would go around, Milking their goats, and he would ask them.

797
00:57:03,805 --> 00:57:08,624
Do you want the milk to have foam on the top or without foam, custom made.

798
00:57:09,087 --> 00:57:12,432
If you want foam that he will lower the cup, or the bowl,

799
00:57:12,655 --> 00:57:15,228
and he will squeeze the milk so that it will make a foam.

800
00:57:15,756 --> 00:57:19,408
If they say we don't want foam, then he will bring it closer to the breast.

801
00:57:20,788 --> 00:57:27,002
He's the Khalifah(خليفه), his armies are shaking the thrones of Persia, and the Roman Empire,

802
00:57:27,217 --> 00:57:29,077
 and he's milking the goats for the old women.

803
00:57:31,855 --> 00:57:38,021
Khalifahرضي الله عنه is comfortable in Madina, going around serving the people,

804
00:57:38,537 --> 00:57:41,717
 while his armies are shaking the thrones of Kuffr(كفر) around the world.

805
00:57:44,012 --> 00:57:48,655
So the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) wasn't a magnificent scene, don't go into these beautiful palaces

806
00:57:50,458 --> 00:57:55,121
decorated with gold and silver with bodyguards surrounding him, from every direction.

807
00:57:55,422 --> 00:58:00,998
You go in, you don't tell the difference between him and everybody else wearing regular clothes.

808
00:58:01,038 --> 00:58:02,295
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying:

809
00:58:02,736 --> 00:58:07,839
Stay away from the clothes of those luxurious people continue with the clothes of your father's.

810
00:58:08,236 --> 00:58:13,598
The poor dress code of two pieces of cloth that you wrapped around your body.

811
00:58:15,532 --> 00:58:20,244
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was the Khalifah(خليفه) and he is speaking to his armies, who are in Azerbaijan.

812
00:58:22,538 --> 00:58:25,012
He, one day went to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), and he said:

813
00:58:25,036 --> 00:58:28,816
Let's go and visit Umm Aimen(أم أيمن) like Rasool Allah ﷺ used to visit her.

814
00:58:29,538 --> 00:58:34,918
Umm Aimen(أم أيمن) nursed Rasool Allah ﷺ she's an Abyssinian slave

815
00:58:36,000 --> 00:58:40,060
and Rasool Allah ﷺ freed her, and he used to love her so much.

816
00:58:40,978 --> 00:58:42,136
And she nursed him.

817
00:58:43,962 --> 00:58:46,379
So she was like, the mother of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

818
00:58:47,538 --> 00:58:51,063
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Let's go and visit her, like Rasool Allah ﷺ used to visit her.

819
00:58:52,575 --> 00:58:56,550
So Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق) and Umar(عُمَر) went to visit this old woman, Umm Aimen(أم أيمن).

820
00:58:57,034 --> 00:58:59,250
 And as soon as, they sat down, she started crying.

821
00:59:00,700 --> 00:59:03,657
So Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Why are you crying?

822
00:59:03,801 --> 00:59:06,726
If Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ has given His Messenger what's better for him.

823
00:59:07,235 --> 00:59:08,863
He thought that she's crying because

824
00:59:10,352 --> 00:59:13,215
it's not Rasool Allah ﷺ who was visiting her, it's Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر).

825
00:59:14,102 --> 00:59:18,248
So he said: Allah has given Rasool Ullah, what is better for him. Why are you crying?

826
00:59:18,721 --> 00:59:23,895
She said: I'm not crying because I don't know that Allah has given His Messenger what's better for him.

827
00:59:23,935 --> 00:59:29,983
 I'm crying because the revelation discontinued by the death of Muhammadﷺ.

828
00:59:30,636 --> 00:59:32,577
Because there's no more Wahee(وحي) coming to us.

829
00:59:33,300 --> 00:59:37,247
And that stirred up the emotion of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Umar(عُمَر) and they cried with her.

830
00:59:40,798 --> 00:59:44,449
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه saw a woman a foreign woman, he doesn't know her.

831
00:59:44,599 --> 00:59:45,437
 Her name is Zainab(زينب).

832
00:59:46,352 --> 00:59:48,363
After a while he noticed that she wasn't speaking.

833
00:59:49,305 --> 00:59:51,747
So he said: What's wrong with this woman, how come she doesn't speak.?

834
00:59:52,908 --> 00:59:53,247
They said:

835
00:59:53,271 --> 00:59:55,530
نذرت أن تحجَّ صامةً

836
00:59:56,026 --> 01:00:03,059
She made an oath, Nadhar(نذر), a vow that she's gonna make Hajj(حَجْ) without speaking.

837
01:00:04,969 --> 01:00:09,089
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه and I'm bringing this up as an example of Naseeha(نصيحة).

838
01:00:10,741 --> 01:00:12,322
He said: تكلمي Speak

839
01:00:12,725 --> 01:00:14,979
فَاِنَهَا هذا لا يحل فإنهم من أمر الجاهلية

840
01:00:15,374 --> 01:00:20,671
Speak! It is not allowed for you to do that, and this is an affair of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

841
01:00:20,769 --> 01:00:24,312
These are things of Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة), making a vow not to speak and -

842
01:00:25,746 --> 01:00:29,132
So, she spoke and said: Who are you? He said:

843
01:00:29,699 --> 01:00:31,272
أن إمراء من المهاجرين

844
01:00:31,542 --> 01:00:34,206
I am a man from among the Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

845
01:00:34,843 --> 01:00:37,792
She said: Which part of Muhajireen(مهاجرين) are you from?

846
01:00:38,288 --> 01:00:39,499
He said: I'm from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

847
01:00:39,685 --> 01:00:41,253
She said: Which part of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) are you from?

848
01:00:41,311 --> 01:00:44,223
He said: إنَّكي لَسئول You asked too many questions.

849
01:00:44,961 --> 01:00:46,794
And in the beginning you don't want to speak at all

850
01:00:46,826 --> 01:00:48,895
and now you just started question, after question

851
01:00:49,345 --> 01:00:51,101
إنَّكي لَسئول أنا ابوبكر

852
01:00:51,511 --> 01:00:55,942
You asked too many questions I am Abu Bakr(ابوبكر). So she said:

853
01:00:55,966 --> 01:00:57,541
يا خليفة الرسول الله

854
01:00:58,404 --> 01:01:01,522
O successor of the Messenger of Allah.

855
01:01:03,753 --> 01:01:10,439
This age of good that we're living in, that came after an Age of Ignorance.

856
01:01:11,640 --> 01:01:13,106
How long will it last.?

857
01:01:14,582 --> 01:01:16,740
This woman lived in the time Jahiliyyah(جَاهلِيَّة).

858
01:01:17,373 --> 01:01:24,493
And she lived in the time of Islam, and she saw the blessing and the Barakah(بركة) of the rule of Allah, the Hukum(حكم) of Allah.

859
01:01:25,493 --> 01:01:26,034
 So she said:

860
01:01:26,059 --> 01:01:30,691
This time of good. How long will it last.?

861
01:01:31,953 --> 01:01:37,796
He said: It will last as long as your Imam(اِمَام)s stick to the straight path.

862
01:01:38,761 --> 01:01:45,427
As long as the Imam(اِمَام)s keep to the straight path, this affair will last.

863
01:01:46,158 --> 01:01:47,528
She said: Who are the Imam(اِمَام)s?

864
01:01:47,568 --> 01:01:49,187
This is a very simple - illiterate woman,

865
01:01:49,239 --> 01:01:50,726
she said: Who are the Imam(اِمَام)s.?

866
01:01:51,940 --> 01:02:00,127
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: Among your people are their heads, and leaders, who when they give orders they are obeyed.?

867
01:02:00,631 --> 01:02:02,910
She said: Yes. He said: Those are the Imam(اِمَام)s.

868
01:02:04,211 --> 01:02:07,083
Anybody in a position of authority, is an Imam(اِمَام).

869
01:02:07,634 --> 01:02:10,175
Anybody who's listened to, is an Imam(اِمَام).

870
01:02:11,053 --> 01:02:13,567
And as long as the Imam(اِمَام)s are on the straight path

871
01:02:13,860 --> 01:02:15,453
the Ummah(امة) will be on the straight path.

872
01:02:18,879 --> 01:02:24,728
He would enjoin good and forbid evil, he would educate the Ummah(امة).

873
01:02:25,419 --> 01:02:27,615
There's an Ayah(آية) in Qur'an, Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says;

874
01:02:28,229 --> 01:02:33,814
يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْفُسَكُمْ لَا يَضُرُّكُمْ مَنْ ضَلَّ إِذَا اهْتَدَيْتُمْ

875
01:02:34,072 --> 01:02:37,761
Al-Maidah(ألمائدة) One O five(105) Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ says: O you, who believed

876
01:02:38,131 --> 01:02:40,908
upon you is responsibility of yourselves

877
01:02:41,389 --> 01:02:45,656
those who have gone astray will not harm you. When you have been guided.

878
01:02:46,504 --> 01:02:49,381
Allah is saying, Take care of yourself.

879
01:02:50,849 --> 01:02:54,132
No matter what happens to the people around you it won't harm you.

880
01:02:54,997 --> 01:03:02,409
Now some people might interpret this as being inactive or or negative and not having any involvement

881
01:03:02,433 --> 01:03:04,513
to just take care of yourself and leave everybody else.

882
01:03:05,009 --> 01:03:07,981
So when Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) felt that some people are giving it, this interpretation.

883
01:03:08,501 --> 01:03:13,412
He gathered them and told them, I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say,

884
01:03:13,744 --> 01:03:18,285
إنَّ القومَ إذا رَأَوُا المُنكَرَ فلَمْ يُغَيِّروهُ؛ عمَّهَمُ اللهُ بعذابٍ

885
01:03:18,922 --> 01:03:23,679
I've heard, Rasool Allah ﷺ say that if people see evil happening in front of their eyes

886
01:03:23,704 --> 01:03:26,421
and they don't prevent it, they will all be punished.

887
01:03:27,214 --> 01:03:29,250
So you have to understand the Ayah(آية) right.

888
01:03:31,191 --> 01:03:32,262
An-Nawawi(ألنووي) says;

889
01:03:32,898 --> 01:03:40,221
وأمَّا قوله تعالىيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا عَلَيْكُمْ أَنْفُسَكُمْ فليس مخالف لوجوب الأمر بالمعروف ونهي عن المنكر

890
01:03:40,647 --> 01:03:44,106
لأنَّ المذهب الصحيح عند المحققين في معنى الآية

891
01:03:44,524 --> 01:03:52,666
أنكم إذا فعلتم ما كلفتم به فلا يضركم  تقسروغيركم مثل قوله تعالى وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ

892
01:03:52,691 --> 01:03:56,820
An-Nawawi(ألنووي) says, when Allah says that O, you who believe,

893
01:03:58,300 --> 01:04:03,185
if you are doing right, it won't harm you in the misguidance of others

894
01:04:03,209 --> 01:04:06,081
it does not mean that you shouldn't enjoin good and forbid evil

895
01:04:07,016 --> 01:04:13,635
but it means that if you forbid evil and you enjoined good

896
01:04:13,983 --> 01:04:17,222
and then the people did not follow it, then that will not harm you.

897
01:04:19,375 --> 01:04:20,809
So At-Taifah Al-Mansoora(ألطائفة المنصورة)

898
01:04:20,833 --> 01:04:22,557
I'm bringing up the At-Taifah Al-Mansoora(ألطائفة المنصورة) a lot

899
01:04:22,581 --> 01:04:24,324
because it's an important concept to understand.

900
01:04:24,348 --> 01:04:26,408
Rasool Allah ﷺ talks about this victorious group.

901
01:04:27,278 --> 01:04:28,630
Rasool Allah ﷺ says about them

902
01:04:28,655 --> 01:04:29,901
لا يضرهم من خلفهم

903
01:04:29,925 --> 01:04:35,077
They are not harmed by the ones, who disagree with them, because they have already done,

904
01:04:35,117 --> 01:04:36,725
 الأمر بالمعروف ونهي عن المنكر

905
01:04:37,010 --> 01:04:40,406
Therefore, whatever anybody else, would do wouldn't harm them.

906
01:04:40,887 --> 01:04:44,757
As long as they have fulfilled their role in enjoining good and forbidding evil.

907
01:04:46,519 --> 01:04:50,679
But if you do not forbid evil and you allow it to happen.

908
01:04:50,766 --> 01:04:52,496
No, you will be harmed by that

909
01:04:53,619 --> 01:04:55,105
وَلَا تَزِرُ وَازِرَةٌ وِزْرَ أُخْرَىٰ

910
01:04:55,129 --> 01:04:58,550
And no bear of burdens shall bear the burden of another.

911
01:05:01,320 --> 01:05:04,719
He would fix the mistakes of others, for example, somebody came in and said;

912
01:05:05,286 --> 01:05:07,433
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was sitting in the gathering, so he came in and said;

913
01:05:07,609 --> 01:05:11,359
ألسلام عليك يا خليفة الرسول الله

914
01:05:12,723 --> 01:05:15,347
Assalam-O-Alaikah, O Khalifah(خليفه) of the Messenger of Allah

915
01:05:15,662 --> 01:05:15,947
he said:

916
01:05:15,971 --> 01:05:17,275
من بيني ها أوْلآءجميعًا

917
01:05:17,599 --> 01:05:19,362
You give me Salam(سلام) out of all of these people

918
01:05:20,553 --> 01:05:23,011
meaning, why just me, why you only give me Salam(سلام).

919
01:05:23,035 --> 01:05:24,486
Say Assalam-O-Alaikum(ألسلام عليكم) to everyone.

920
01:05:24,946 --> 01:05:26,653
He told his son Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن)

921
01:05:26,854 --> 01:05:29,831
ولا تمازجارك فإنَّ هذا يبقى ويذهب الناس

922
01:05:30,562 --> 01:05:34,634
Don't fight with your neighbor, because this will remain, and people will die.

923
01:05:35,686 --> 01:05:39,190
You will die and your neighbor will die but your deeds will remain.

924
01:05:39,757 --> 01:05:41,902
So don't fight with your neighbor and be nice.

925
01:05:42,195 --> 01:05:46,352
This is permanent, what you do is permanent, and it will be remembered by people,

926
01:05:46,417 --> 01:05:51,557
and it will be brought up by Allahعَزَّوَجَلْ on the day of judgment, but you will die and your neighbor will die.

927
01:05:51,944 --> 01:05:56,428
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسلِيْمًا كثيرا

